{
  "duration": 79.279,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.079,
      "end": 0.819,
      "text": "So welcome back."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.379,
      "end": 3.74,
      "text": "I hope you have gone through the theory part for this topic."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.139,
      "end": 5.819,
      "text": "Now it's time to solve some problems."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.359,
      "end": 10.939,
      "text": "In this problem, we are given the area of a square as one hundred forty-four square centimeter,"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.46,
      "end": 12.899,
      "text": "and we need to find its perimeter."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.399,
      "end": 13.579,
      "text": "Now,"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.059,
      "end": 15.439,
      "text": "what does perimeter mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.96,
      "end": 19.959,
      "text": "It is simply the total length of all four sides of the square."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.479,
      "end": 24.519,
      "text": "So to find the perimeter, we first need to find the length of one side."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.959,
      "end": 25.459,
      "text": "Correct?"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.119,
      "end": 29.399,
      "text": "We know that area of a square equal to side square,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.899,
      "end": 33.439,
      "text": "and the area is given as one hundred forty-four."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.0,
      "end": 36.219,
      "text": "So side square equal to one hundred"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.68,
      "end": 37.319,
      "text": "forty-four."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.639,
      "end": 39.139,
      "text": "Now ask yourself a simple question:"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.659,
      "end": 41.939,
      "text": "Which number, when multiplied by itself,"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.34,
      "end": 45.079,
      "text": "gives one hundred forty-four? It is twelve,"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.52,
      "end": 49.739,
      "text": "because twelve times twelve equal to one hundred forty-four."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.239,
      "end": 53.879,
      "text": "So the side of the square is twelve centimeter."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.759,
      "end": 56.059,
      "text": "Got it? Perfect."
    },
    {
      "start": 56.719,
      "end": 60.239,
      "text": "Now that we have the side, finding the perimeter is very easy."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.879,
      "end": 79.279,
      "text": "Perimeter of a square equal to four times side. Why four? Because a square has four equal sides. So perimeter equal to four times twelve, which gives us forty-eight centimeter. Done and dusted. So the final answer will be forty-eight centimeter. Hence, option C is the correct answer"
    }
  ],
